-- #964 (2026-10-28): walk links whose stored path crosses ground the 5.4.8 navmesh does not have (playerbots DB).
--
-- 1000-bot run mop1k-v4-1028 (first hour): 28 stuck-teleport walk-stall / 10 abandon walk-stall. Every stall target
-- was looked up in playerbots_travelnode_path and its link checked offline against the servers own mmaps
-- (the extracted 5.4.8 client data; (not shipped) tg_nav / tg_check). The
-- hotspot, map 1 (1590.5,-576.7,77.1) = point 27 of 2328 Stonetalon The Talondeep Path -> 2324 Ashenvale The
-- Talondeep Path (also 2328 -> 2249 / 3008 and 2324 -> 2328), is ACs WotLK tunnel: 73-75 consecutive points from
-- x 1543 to 1907 have no walkable poly within 8 yd / 15 yd vertical (the 5.4.8 navmesh there is the surface, z 98-225,
-- or nothing), so bots stalled at the tunnel mouth and the stuck teleport put them inside the rock. The 5.4.8
-- navmesh links 2328 and 2324 by the pass to the north (y -430..-470, 764 yd). Most other stalls of the hour sit on
-- links with the same defect (Darkshore 3470 -> 3003, Orgrimmar 370 / 426 <-> 537, Thousand Needles 2510 -> 3517,
-- Stonetalon 2959 <-> 3033 / 3486, Wetlands 186 <-> 3533 / 3536, Dun Morogh 3081 -> 2663, Orgrimmar 2091 -> 1713, ...).
--
-- Audit of every walk link (type 1) on maps 0 / 1 / 530 / 571 (10802 links): a link is defective when 3 or more
-- consecutive interior path points have no walkable poly (bot filter: ground + water, no magma / slime) within 3 yd
-- / 5 yd vertical - the findNearestPoly box PathGenerator tries first. 901 links. Links touching the nodes that
-- 2026_10_28_02.sql re-walks or deletes (39 211 271 646 669 620 629 1962 1968) are left to that file, and links touching
-- a transport dock node (any type 3 link, 37) are left as they are (their water / pier ends are #948 / #956 territory).
--  * Rebuilt: 792 links (map 0: 287, 1: 423, 530: 67, 571: 15): Detour A* between the two node positions with the bot
--    filter (water area cost 20), funnel, points every <= 15 yd, the exact node positions as first / last point;
--    distance / swim_distance by AC TravelNodePath::calculateCost (distance from 0.1). type / object / extra_cost /
--    max_creature_* keep their values. Every other link is unchanged.
--  * Deleted: 51 links (map 0: 31, 1: 20) whose two nodes the navmesh does not connect at all (A* over 800000 polys),
--    only where the graph keeps the same strongly connected components and both nodes keep a link out / in;
--    17 such links are kept because removing them would cut the graph; 10 links with a node off the navmesh are kept.
--  * Deleted: the Telredor elevator 183177 links (1973 <-> 1974, 1974 <-> 1975, 1975 -> 1973). No bot boarded it in any
--    log of 2026-10-27/28 (4 waits, 0 boards): at the bottom stop the platform stands at z 27.0-27.5 and the only
--    navmesh around the shaft is the ground at z 18.9, so FindDeckPoint never sees the deck (wait-why no-deck-point,
--    dock-approach-level no-ground, dock-wait-timeout after 720 s: Merlios, Ival, Lunasaana; Emerlo at the top stop).
--    Telredor stays reachable by its flight master.
-- Apply after 2026_10_28_02.sql / 2026_10_28_03.sql. Re-runnable: every pair is DELETEd before it is written.
-- Undo: (not shipped) (the rows as they were on the test
-- a local DB on 2026-10-28, before this file).
-- Generator: (not shipped) (tg_nav.py, tg_work.walk_job, tg_sql.walk_cost) driven by
-- the #964 audit / rebuild / emit scripts (copied to (not shipped).

